To verify whether a pattern is matched on a given board, we rst extend the
board borders with walls and then check for each possible pattern location that
every cell are compatible as dened by Table 2. For instance, if the attacking
player is White, then a White pawn will match any cell type in the pattern. Put
another way, if the pattern cell corresponding to a Black pawn is not Crossable
or Don't Care, then the pattern does not match.
